From f17eb2b57b7b0c0f6639ea3f7cf3c2b61dec8e0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:39:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): bound opted-in pre-swap stop across discovery,
 RPC and dispatch; Linux-only; refuse unmanageable gateways [daveey]

One absolute 30s deadline now clamps discovery subprocesses and the cgroup escape wait,
the control-socket exchange (single transport deadline), and every systemctl/kill dispatch
(no 0.1s floor; nothing issued once expired). Discovery timeouts refuse instead of
returning a smaller set. Opted-in gateways the update cannot stop refuse rather than
print-and-continue. macOS stays idle-only. Recovery is announced as its own phase.
